# S1 delicacy proof pairs: deterministic re-renders (degrade stage), not the pool of record
public/audio/delicacy/proof-*
# E4/E5 staircase pool — THE DIRECTORY STAYS IGNORED, AND THE SHIPPING CLIPS ARE
# TRACKED ANYWAY (PM ruling RT-94a b, 2026-08-20; supersedes RT-71b's "not yet").
#
# 486 files sit here after a render. Exactly 400 of them — 129.6 MB — are the ones a
# session or the Lab can name, and those are committed with `git add -f`. gitignore
# does not un-track a tracked file, so they clone and they deploy; the rule only
# governs what happens to files nobody has decided about yet.
#
# THE DIRECTORY IS IGNORED ON PURPOSE, and it is not an oversight to be tidied up.
# This is a PUBLIC repo: a commit here is permanent, and `git add -A` after a re-render
# would sweep in the 86 files that must never ship — 66 orphans no code path names, and
# 20 timing clips on pb1@120s / pb6@75s whose drift trajectory the correlator could not
# verify (RT-75a). `clipFor` refuses to hand those back; publishing them would put
# stimuli on a CDN whose labels the audio itself does not corroborate.
#
# To add clips after a re-render: regenerate the reachable set from the engine and
# `git add -f` exactly that list. A comment cannot enforce this and `staircase-shipping.
# test.ts` does: it fails if a reachable clip is untracked, and it ALSO fails if anything
# untracked-for-a-reason gets swept in. Both directions are proven by mutation, so if you
# are reading this because that test is red, believe it.
#
# AND THEN THE PUSH WILL FAIL, which is worth knowing before you spend an hour on it.
# A ~130 MB pack over HTTPS dies with `RPC failed; HTTP 408` — twice, here, including
# once with http.postBuffer raised to 500 MB, which is the fix everyone suggests and
# does not work. There is no SSH remote on this machine. What works: push the blobs
# ahead of the real commit in chunks, on a throwaway ref, then push the real branch
# against a remote that already has them (its pack is then a few KB).
#
#   git ls-tree -r <commit> -- public/audio/staircase > /tmp/blobs.txt
#   split -l 50 -d /tmp/blobs.txt /tmp/chunk_
#   GIT_INDEX_FILE=/tmp/chunk.idx  # never touches your working tree or HEAD
#   read-tree the base commit, then per chunk: update-index --add --cacheinfo,
#   write-tree, commit-tree, update-ref refs/heads/tmp-audio-upload, push
#   finally: push the real branch, then `git push origin --delete tmp-audio-upload`
#
# 50 files (~16 MB) per chunk went up first try, 8 for 8. The throwaway commits are
# unreferenced afterwards and GitHub garbage-collects them, so history keeps exactly
# one audio commit.
public/audio/staircase/
